{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"alabaster-hairy-limpet","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observation\n\n`show_ticket` always computes `inbound_deps` by byte-scanning every event file in the store (src/rebar/reducer/_inbound.py, lines 39-72). On a clone of the live store, 2026-10-29, that is 139,978 files and 609 MB read per call. Only CREATE, EDIT, LINK, UNLINK and SNAPSHOT events change deps or parent (src/rebar/reducer/_replay.py). Restricting the scan to those types read 13,258 files and 150.5 MB, and found all 15 confirmed inbound links for the 1 ticket tested.\n\nCaveats:\n- The scan trusts that the filename suffix matches the event type inside the file.\n- Link targets are stored as written, so a link stored by alias is missed by an id byte scan. That gap exists in the current scan too; on the clone, 2 of 1,605 LINK targets are not canonical ids, and both are free text.\n\n## Plan\n1. Restrict the inbound scan to the relationship-bearing event types by filename suffix.\n2. Add a test that puts a link in each relationship event type and checks each is still found, plus one where a COMMENT body names the target and must not produce a false candidate.\n3. Compare the inbound_deps of a sample of live-store tickets before and after on a clone.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The scan opens only CREATE, EDIT, LINK, UNLINK and SNAPSHOT event files.\n- [ ] inbound_deps is identical to the current code for at least 50 tickets sampled from a clone of the live store.\n\n## File impact (expected)\n- src/rebar/reducer/_inbound.py","id":"0076-375d-430c-4822","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"show_ticket's inbound-link scan reads every event file in the store"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793301736491063001,"uuid":"5dddbd90-ebb4-4ca0-9980-afbf38f9c35e"}